WEBVTT

1
00:00:13.095 --> 00:00:16.276
smiled as Zing shot another burst of flame at Zann.

2
00:00:16.816 --> 00:00:18.916
"Good old Zing," she thought.

3
00:00:19.396 --> 00:00:20.997
Then her smile faded.

4
00:00:21.717 --> 00:00:24.178
She was troubled by what Mellis had just told them.

5
00:00:24.198 --> 00:00:28.199
"I don't care much about what happens to Vilkor," she thought.

6
00:00:28.219 --> 00:00:32.872
"But Mellis cares about him, and I care about Mellis.

7
00:00:32.892 --> 00:00:37.133
Zann and I haven't known her that long, but she already feels like a true friend."

8
00:00:37.153 --> 00:00:44.295
"Let's decide what to do," she said after Zing settled down, and Zann magically healed his burns.

9
00:00:46.316 --> 00:00:51.937
"Should we return to Magica, or stay and try to convince Zira to share the truth about magic

10
00:00:51.957 --> 00:00:52.617
with everyone?"

11
00:00:53.458 --> 00:00:54.198
Zann shrugged.

12
00:00:54.218 --> 00:00:57.659
"I don't like the thought of Zira and Vilkor running things.

13
00:00:58.459 --> 00:00:59.479
But it's not our world.

14
00:01:00.100 --> 00:01:01.380
Maybe it's none of our business."

15
00:01:02.256 --> 00:01:03.957
Perda felt more troubled than ever.

16
00:01:04.517 --> 00:01:05.397
Could Zann be right?

17
00:01:05.417 --> 00:01:12.220
"If Mellis can convince her uncle and Zira to rule for the benefit of all, maybe it wouldn't

18
00:01:12.260 --> 00:01:14.061
be so bad," she said.

19
00:01:14.081 --> 00:01:17.283
"But still, leaving now doesn't seem right."

20
00:01:18.003 --> 00:01:20.104
She glanced over to see what Mellis thought.

21
00:01:20.604 --> 00:01:22.465
But Mellis hardly seemed to be listening.

22
00:01:23.125 --> 00:01:24.466
She was gazing out the window.

23
00:01:24.486 --> 00:01:25.606
"What's wrong?"

24
00:01:26.087 --> 00:01:26.727
Perda asked.

25
00:01:27.447 --> 00:01:28.187
Mellis sighed.

26
00:01:30.136 --> 00:01:32.578
"I was just thinking about the pendant I lost."

27
00:01:33.799 --> 00:01:36.762
Perda recalled hearing Mellis mention that she'd lost something.

28
00:01:36.782 --> 00:01:38.423
"What kind of pendant?"

29
00:01:38.884 --> 00:01:39.344
she asked.

30
00:01:39.364 --> 00:01:44.448
"It was the only thing I still had that belonged to my mother," Mellis said sadly.

31
00:01:44.468 --> 00:01:47.971
"I noticed it was gone shortly after you two arrived.

32
00:01:48.732 --> 00:01:51.254
I must have broken the cord while digging the well."

33
00:01:51.274 --> 00:01:54.937
"We could zap out there later and help you search," Zann said.

34
00:01:54.957 --> 00:01:57.660
"We should probably check on the wormhole anyway."

35
00:01:58.348 --> 00:02:02.191
"We haven't decided yet if we're leaving right away," Perda reminded him.

36
00:02:02.211 --> 00:02:04.273
"I know," Zann said.

37
00:02:04.293 --> 00:02:07.256
"But we don't even know if we can get to the wormhole by the well.

38
00:02:07.896 --> 00:02:11.079
If we can't, we'll have to zap all the way back out to the mines."

39
00:02:11.800 --> 00:02:12.480
"The mines?"

40
00:02:13.021 --> 00:02:13.681
Mellis echoed.

41
00:02:13.701 --> 00:02:14.882
"What do you mean?"

42
00:02:15.683 --> 00:02:21.248
While Zann told her about the wormhole he'd discovered near the mines, Perda paced the room and thought

43
00:02:21.268 --> 00:02:22.028
about what to do.

44
00:02:22.729 --> 00:02:25.712
She didn't trust Zira, or Vilkor, for that matter.

45
00:02:26.520 --> 00:02:31.264
How could they even think about leaving Mellis—and all of Terrica—in their greedy hands?

46
00:02:32.625 --> 00:02:37.669
She was still pondering the same question a few hours later at a sumptuous feast in the banquet

47
00:02:37.689 --> 00:02:40.291
hall that overlooked Zira's courtyard garden.

48
00:02:40.952 --> 00:02:46.796
The purple berries on the bush outside seemed to glow as a moon rose in the darkening sky.

49
00:02:47.237 --> 00:02:48.618
Zann pushed back his chair.

50
00:02:48.638 --> 00:02:51.840
"I'd better take Zing for a walk," he said to Zira.

51
00:02:52.501 --> 00:02:56.284
"He gets restless and starts setting things on fire if he's kept indoors for too long.

52
00:02:56.896 --> 00:02:57.716
May I be excused?"

53
00:02:57.736 --> 00:03:04.018
"Of course," Zira said before returning her attention to her conversation with the woman beside her.

54
00:03:04.798 --> 00:03:11.180
A few minutes later, Mellis excused herself as well, saying she wanted to prepare sleeping chambers for Perda

55
00:03:11.340 --> 00:03:11.860
and Zann.

56
00:03:12.420 --> 00:03:15.721
Perda forced herself to wait several more minutes before standing up.

57
00:03:15.741 --> 00:03:21.483
"I'm exhausted," she said, faking a yawn.

58
00:03:21.503 --> 00:03:24.464
"I think I'll head straight to bed."

59
00:03:25.504 --> 00:03:28.386
She hurried outside and found Zann and Mellis waiting.

60
00:03:29.147 --> 00:03:30.048
Zing was there too.

61
00:03:30.068 --> 00:03:33.150
"Are you sure we should bring him?"

62
00:03:33.631 --> 00:03:36.573
she asked as the little dragon flew in a circle overhead.

63
00:03:36.593 --> 00:03:39.135
"He tends to attract attention."

64
00:03:39.155 --> 00:03:42.918
"I'm not leaving him behind again," Zann said.

65
00:03:43.679 --> 00:03:44.339
Perda shrugged.

66
00:03:44.359 --> 00:03:45.801
"Okay, you're right.

67
00:03:46.341 --> 00:03:48.183
We should stick together from now on."

68
00:03:49.003 --> 00:03:50.204
They zapped to the well.

69
00:03:50.785 --> 00:03:54.608
The villagers were gone, but the area wasn't completely deserted.

70
00:03:55.504 --> 00:03:59.345
A pack of gorzogs was there, circling a large metal cage.

71
00:03:59.965 --> 00:04:06.347
A man cowered inside the cage, dodging as the gorzogs occasionally stuck a clawed paw in to try

72
00:04:06.387 --> 00:04:06.927
to grab him.

73
00:04:06.947 --> 00:04:10.268
"It's Trof, the plonk farmer!"

74
00:04:10.808 --> 00:04:11.448
Perda cried.

75
00:04:12.209 --> 00:04:14.929
Trof stared at the kids with terror in his eyes.

76
00:04:15.670 --> 00:04:19.191
There was a long scratch on his face and another on his arm.

77
00:04:19.211 --> 00:04:21.091
"Help me!"

78
00:04:21.651 --> 00:04:22.071
he cried.

79
00:04:22.752 --> 00:04:24.580
Perda didn't like Trof.

80
00:04:24.600 --> 00:04:26.541
But she hated to see anyone suffer.

81
00:04:27.141 --> 00:04:28.322
She rubbed her hands together.

82
00:04:28.342 --> 00:04:30.103
"Get out of here!"

83
00:04:30.643 --> 00:04:34.105
she yelled as she sent several fireballs toward the gorzogs.

84
00:04:34.966 --> 00:04:38.127
The creatures jumped in surprise and dodged the fireballs.

85
00:04:39.048 --> 00:04:40.048
But they didn't run away.

86
00:04:40.809 --> 00:04:46.072
Perda and Zann tried creating a loud horn sound next and then bright, flashing lights.

87
00:04:47.292 --> 00:04:49.494
"Stop," Mellis cried, pointing.

88
00:04:49.514 --> 00:04:51.595
"All you're doing is attracting more!

89
00:04:51.855 --> 00:04:53.536
Gorzogs are practically fearless."

90
00:04:54.412 --> 00:04:59.897
Perda glanced toward the horizon, where more gorzogs were creeping into view out of the darkness.

91
00:04:59.917 --> 00:05:02.919
"We'd better zap away," she said.

92
00:05:02.939 --> 00:05:06.061
"Maybe we can figure out how to zap this guy with us."

93
00:05:06.081 --> 00:05:08.623
"No, wait," Zann said.

94
00:05:08.644 --> 00:05:12.387
"The gorzogs seemed to react to Zing's song before, remember?

95
00:05:13.207 --> 00:05:14.308
Zing! Try singing!"

96
00:05:14.989 --> 00:05:16.650
The little dragon started whistling.

97
00:05:17.531 --> 00:05:18.972
At first nothing happened.

98
00:05:20.140 --> 00:05:26.082
"A fire whistler's song doesn't usually work on otherworldly creatures," Perda reminded Zann.

99
00:05:26.843 --> 00:05:28.163
"Wait," Mellis said.

100
00:05:28.183 --> 00:05:32.585
"Look!" One of the gorzogs had stopped to stare up at Zing.

101
00:05:33.325 --> 00:05:34.766
Several others did the same.

102
00:05:35.406 --> 00:05:36.867
Their eyes were glassy.

103
00:05:37.447 --> 00:05:41.709
A couple of them drooled slightly as they swayed in time with the dragon's song.

104
00:05:41.729 --> 00:05:43.690
"It's working!"

105
00:05:44.210 --> 00:05:45.050
Perda exclaimed.

106
00:05:45.790 --> 00:05:47.571
She and Zann rushed to the cage.

107
00:05:48.191 --> 00:05:52.177
As soon as Trof was free, he raced away without even thanking the kids.

108
00:05:52.197 --> 00:05:54.838
"Let's get out of here," Zann said.

109
00:05:54.858 --> 00:05:57.279
"We'll come back later when the gorzogs are gone."

110
00:05:58.079 --> 00:06:00.701
Perda nodded, but Mellis didn't respond.

111
00:06:01.541 --> 00:06:04.322
She appeared to be listening carefully to Zing's song.

112
00:06:05.062 --> 00:06:08.364
Then she opened her mouth—and started to sing!

113
00:06:09.284 --> 00:06:12.665
Her voice echoed the dragon's song almost perfectly!

114
00:06:13.766 --> 00:06:15.006
The gorzogs heard it too.

115
00:06:15.607 --> 00:06:18.688
They swayed and turned to face her adoringly.

116
00:06:19.708 --> 00:06:23.751
After a moment Mellis stepped forward and patted one on its scruffy head!
